              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "17. Without the salt bridge, the circuit would be open (or broken) and no current could flow. With a salt bridge, each half-cell remains electrically neutral and current can flow through the circuit."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "de366075e60342b6b4000d6df99e2f1c",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "x5814adwq4u6000",
                "type": "li"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "19. Active electrodes participate in the oxidation-reduction reaction. Since metals form cations, the electrode would lose mass if metal atoms in the electrode were to oxidize and go into solution. Oxidation occurs at the anode."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "b6ee5f74750347a3b826648abb871ce5",
                    "type": "p"
